Suppose f:X ⊆ R^n -> R is a scalar-calued function of n variables. 
Let x = (x₁, x₂, ..., x(sub(n))) denote a point of R^n. 
A partial function F with repspect to the variable x(sub(i)) is a one-variable function obtained from f by holding all variables constant except x(sub(i)). 
That is, we set x(sub(j)) equal to a constant a(sub(j)) for j != i. 
Then the partial function in x(sub(i)) is defined by 

		F(x(sub(i))) = (a₁, a₂, ..., a(sub(n)))
